# nr-office-engine-snapshot: the snapshot action of the office engine (module mixdog-office::snapshot)

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled (rustfmt parsed every file). The module is a library the Office tool's
service (a later task of the office track) calls; this task registers no protocol method and no service, so nothing is removed
from SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod session;` add (and extend the crate doc by one line: "[`snapshot`] reads a session's document as the model sees it: page
requests and cursors, the review of what the document says to the agent, query, the snapshot contract."):

    pub mod snapshot;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], after `mixdog-office-base`:

    mixdog-office-com = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-pdf = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-quality = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-ooxml = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies]:

    mixdog-fonts = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-pdf = { workspace = true }

(`mixdog-fsio`, `mixdog-js`, `mixdog-office-base`, `mixdog-office-design`, `mixdog-rt`, `serde_json`, `tempfile` and `tokio` with `rt` are in the
manifest already. None of the four new normal dependencies depends on mixdog-office: mixdog-office-quality has mixdog-office-author as a
dev-dependency only. All six are [workspace.dependencies] entries and members already. No external crate enters the lock.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock
Package `mixdog-office`: add the dependencies mixdog-office-com, mixdog-office-pdf, mixdog-office-quality, mixdog-ooxml and (dev) mixdog-fonts,
mixdog-pdf (`cargo update -w` offline).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing by hand: no new external crate, no new feature. Run the hakari check after the manifest edit and take its output if it asks for a line.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json (the index of the fixture sets)
Add to `sets` (after "office-sessions" or wherever "office-snapshot" sorts):

    { "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-snapshot.mjs --tree <tree>", "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-snapshot/MANIFEST.json", "manifestSha256": "99fc79d4c05eb8dca62f25760de2a01063f87ae96d2356e9b13979f2e2f0be1a",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-snapshot.mjs", "set": "office-snapshot", "totalBytes": 420301 }

(the fixture folder is not checked out in an engineer's worktree: native/core/fixtures/office-snapshot/{golden.json,MANIFEST.json} were
written at their paths and added with `git add --sparse`; re-record with the recorder if the hash differs.)

## Interface the tool layer calls (crate mixdog-office, `mixdog_office::snapshot`)
- `snapshot(&SnapshotContext, &SessionHandle, args: &Value, full: bool) -> Result<Value, String>` (async: only the Office host's answers are
  awaited) and `trust_for_mutation(&SnapshotContext, &SessionHandle) -> Result<Value, String>`.
- `SnapshotContext { proof: &P (a WriteProof), measurer: &TextMeasurer, forms: &dyn FormView, com: &H: ComHost }`; `impl ComHost for
  mixdog_office_com::OfficeCom` is in the module. The future is not Send (the text measurer holds a cache cell): drive it on the lane thread.
- `read_com_saved_copy(cx, handle, read)`: `readComSavedCopy` (the live document saved to a copy that is removed afterwards). It lives here
  because the snapshot of a protected sheet needs it; the open/create task (which the plan lists for it) must reuse this one, not write a second.
- `create_office_snapshot_request`, `finalize_office_snapshot_page` (cursors), `query_object`, `find_by_document_path`,
  `snapshot_selection_for_target`, `office_snapshot_contract_violations`, `describe_office_snapshot_violations`,
  `normalize_excel_snapshot_styles`.
- The tool layer passes the lock-free parts: the session lock is taken only briefly (never across the host's answer).

## Not in this task
`materializeWorkingCopy` (listed with lines 690-935 of office-sessions.mjs but owned, with `readComSavedCopy`, by nr-office-engine-open-create in
the plan's own list) is not ported here: it needs a document-index removal the registry does not have.
